BT 1 0 0 1 36 430.1 Tm /F2 8.5 Tf 10.2 TL (# Mission 004 Coordinator Handoff) Tj T*  T* (## Current mission state) Tj T* (Mission 004 is the live-truth ingestion and storytelling mission.) Tj T* (The mission is now complete: the live source was refreshed again in the repo with a new verification event, production is ingesting the refreshed feed, and the single timeline still shows the latest mission with freshness lag visible.) Tj T*  T* (## What is done) Tj T* (- Mission packet is defined) Tj T* (- Backend, frontend, QA, and coordinator responsibilities are declared) Tj T* (- The release goal is explicit: updated truth plus clearer story, not just a frozen production snapshot) Tj T* (- The writing contract is defined: updates should say what changed, who changed it, why it matters, and what comes next when relevant) Tj T* (- The repo-backed live source snapshot now includes Mission 004 as the latest mission) Tj T* (- Backend and frontend implementation work is reflected in the live source refresh and the follow-up verification event) Tj T* (- Repo checks are green: tests, typecheck, and build pass) Tj T* (- This run revalidated the local repo successfully with `npm test`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run build`) Tj T* (- This run rechecked production and confirmed the deployed app serves Mission 004 data from the refreshed canonical live source) Tj T*  T* (## What remains) Tj T* (- No functional blocker remains for Mission 004) Tj T* (- Keep the freshness state visible and keep the live source refreshed as new truth arrives) Tj T* (- Keep the production deployment path and external live-source wiring documented for future runs) Tj T*  T* (## Coordinator instructions) Tj T* (- Keep the user-facing experience to one live timeline only) Tj T* (- Do not add a second summary view) Tj T* (- Preserve explicit freshness / lag indicators) Tj T* (- Keep the checkpoint updated after each meaningful milestone) Tj T* (- Use the checkpoint and handoffs as the source of truth for future resumption) Tj T* (- Treat Mission 004 as complete unless new scope is introduced) Tj T* (- Send a short update after every meaningful step, not only at the end of a run) Tj T* (- Each update should say who worked and what the next step is) Tj T* (- Every product, backend, frontend, and QA step must be documented in a PDF artifact in the repo at `docs/missions/pdfs/`) Tj T*  T* (## Live runtime note) Tj T* (- Dev server may still be used for local verification) Tj T* (- Production verification must happen on the deployed app) Tj T* (- Production is reachable and returns 200, and the live payload now reflects Mission 004 from the refreshed canonical live source) Tj T* (- Local verification now pins the route test to `AGENTS_VIS_DASHBOARD_SOURCE_FILE=src/lib/dashboard-live-source.json` so the checkout matches the shipped source) Tj T* (- Production smoke this run:) Tj T* (  - `GET https://agents-vis.vercel.app/api/missions/latest` ) Tj /F3 8.5 Tf 10.2 TL (\256) Tj /F2 8.5 Tf 10.2 TL ( 200, Mission 004 payload, `eventCount: 7`, `freshnessState: stale`, `lagMs: 2164553`) Tj T* (  - `GET https://agents-vis.vercel.app/api/dashboard` ) Tj /F3 8.5 Tf 10.2 TL (\256) Tj /F2 8.5 Tf 10.2 TL ( 200, JSON source freshness stale, `lagMs: 2171520`) Tj T* (- The deployed app still serves the single latest-mission timeline through the live source path) Tj T* (- Markdown handoff updated and the matching PDF artifact was regenerated in `docs/missions/pdfs/`) Tj T* ET
